    \"ulid\": \"01KJ8NDTW6M80T7T07SACEP7F8\",\n      \"title\": \"Tests fail when run inside ralph loop due to environment contamination: (1) ralph.test.ts KSPEC_RALPH_SESSION assertion expects null but env var is inherited from ralph process, (2) session-create.test.ts active session warning in stderr breaks JSON parsing, (3) session-budget-integration.test.ts references nonexistent task set-automation command. Tests should isolate from parent process env vars (KSPEC_RALPH_SESSION, KSPEC_SESSION_ID) to be reliable in all contexts.\",\n      \"matchedFields\": [\n        \"text\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"inbox\",\n      \"ulid\": \"01KJG5A7Q8WZDHNTH9M600RZZ9\",\n      \"title\": \"Task budget false-positive outside ralph loop when stale KSPEC_SESSION_ID is present (observed in codex session). Repro: with KSPEC_SESSION_ID set to an old session that has budget.json started_this_cycle=max_per_cycle, 'kspec task start @ref' fails with 'Task budget exhausted ... let iteration end naturally' even when not running ralph and no in-progress tasks. Expected: budget guard should apply only during active ralph loop iteration context, or stale/non-ralph session IDs should be ignored.\",\n      \"matchedFields\": [\n        \"text\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"total\": 28,\n  \"showing\": 28\n}\n","status":"completed"}